  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes: 7 tests, 0 failed, including 5 new regression tests.\n\n**Causes and fixes**\n- **Hang after a failure:** a rejected job never decremented `running`, so its slot was never freed. A job that threw synchronously, or returned a plain value, also crashed `fn().then`. Each job is now wrapped so every outcome counts as a settled job, and the slot is always freed before the next job starts.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending, so it resolved while jobs were still running. It now also requires `running === 0`.\n- **Only one job after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started a single job per call. It is now a loop that fills every free slot, so concurrency 4 gets four jobs running after `resume()`.\n\nThe new tests in `test/queue.test.js` cover:\n- the queue continuing after an async rejection, a synchronous throw and a plain return value;\n- `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs, resolving immediately when idle, and resolving after a failed job;\n- `resume()` filling all free slots;\n- `pause()` letting running jobs finish while holding back new ones.\n\nI didn't run the new tests against the old code to confirm they fail there.",
